{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum","id":1052537,"title":"help with paradox of time arcanum","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-21T06:44:41-08:00","id":1052537,"title":"help with paradox of time arcanum","content":"hi guys<br /> yesterday we played another session, and, because it s the first time we r playing mage ( after have played only vampire the masquerade for lot of times after D&amp;D for a lot of years), one of my player was forced to paradox, multiple time. last time i rolled 8 dice and after mana spent and wisom roll, 2 successes occured<br /> <br /> disclaimer: just to note why he was forced to paradox<br /> the setting is 1817, london, but now they are in french<br /> this player has the time arcanum. They were traking down their foe (a mage), and the journey conducted them to an ancient graveyard where the enemy went the day before, doing a ritual to open a gate and travel through the death realm ( underground?). He left there some anchored ghosts to inform him in case someone investigates in this place.<br /> So, they walk around talking with people in the graveyard and doing some searches through the area. Then, one of them use his power to ask some stuff to the ghosts ( there is a werewolf in the group that can see ghosts and speak with them). Of course, the ghosts warned their master, but they didn t know this.<br /> After a couple of hours, during the night, they came back to graveyard and used their death spells to speak another time with ghosts and they realize that they were there for a reason. But the ghosts tried to stop them, fighting them and when the stuff started to going bad for players, the time arcanum player used &quot;shifting sands&quot; to go back &quot;before&quot; they spoke with ghosts. Some paradoxes occured, but he managed to absorbe.<br /> When they back to rest, they realized that the werewolf spoke with ghosts hours before and he tried to &quot;shifting sands&quot; again, apllying more reaches and creating a paradox. After roll, i did 2 successes and the spell was successfully casted<br /> <br /> now, it s the first time that paradox occured, and i wanna give them the feel that is not safe to play too much with magic and paradox. Beside, i won t admit the rule to scratch the condition from this soul and i still wanna aplly anomalies<br /> i have some nasty ideas, but i wish to hear other thoughts about you can manage a situation like this<br /> don t get me wrong: i don t wanna punish my player for this good tactics, but i don t even wanna see him having a &quot; gold card&quot; to use any time he wants. Of course, stuff will happen later, but for now, i m just happy to apply some nasty effects to him<br /> thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T08:56:11-08:00","id":1052588,"title":"","content":"Did he release or contain the Paradox? If he released it you have Reaches you can choose to apply to or negate from his spell. If he contained you have a few Paradox Conditions you can choose to apply to him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T09:31:02-08:00","id":1052604,"title":"","content":"he cointained it, but i still wanna apply the anomalies even if shouldn t be applied<br /> now, i have to reaches and one condition to apply..<br /> here my thought:<br /> the group is formed by 3 people, 2 mages and one werewolf<br /> now, the 2 mages had lived last 2 in-game years togheter, they know each others very well and they are friends. The werewolf instead, is the new entry by preview session and they are just knowing him. My idea is to spend one reach to change the target from the player that cast it to the werewolf. In this way he has to explain to his new friend what happened and have to be believed by them in wich they don t trust very much. This is the first part<br /> with the second reach i have no idea what to do<br /> for the conditions, i wish to create some temporal loop that affect the player who launched the spell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:19:41-08:00","id":1052618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1052604#post1052604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">he cointained it, but i still wanna apply the anomalies even if shouldn t be applied</div> </div> </div> </div>The context seems like a fantastic excuse to work in Weirdly Otherworldy Omen Dogs as a recurring problem for the character.<br /> <br /> H A U N T <span style=\"color:#D3D3D3\">_</span> H I M","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:32:21-08:00","id":1052628,"title":"","content":"No excuses. In my hoping on paradoxes should be quite terrifying. I can t see any problem casting paradoxes.. The other version of mage punished more who abuses of paradoxes.. <br /> And btw, what is otherworldly omen dogs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T10:50:36-08:00","id":1052634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1052628#post1052628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And btw, what is otherworldly omen dogs?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barghest\" target=\"_blank\">something</a> of a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_Shuck\" target=\"_blank\">general</a> recurring <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Black_dog_(ghost)\" target=\"_blank\">phenomenon</a> in folklore, particularly around Great Britain \u2014 the Grim from Harry Potter draws on the same concept.<br /> <br /> It's particularly salient here because there are at least two Lodges of werewolves who hunt prey that messes with time, one of which (the Tindalosi) is a <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hounds_of_Tindalos\" target=\"_blank\">Lovecraft reference</a>. (Though I admittedly have a very tiny <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/201675-idigam-chronicle-weekly-discussion-hunting-grounds?p=243976#post243976\">personal stake</a> in the concept.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:17:41-08:00","id":1052646,"title":"","content":"Why are you asking about the rules if you want to do something no matter what you learn? If it's what you think is good for the story, the go for it. Keep in mind that doing this even after the player chose how they wanted to deal with the paradox is taking away player agency and choice, railroading them into the story that you want regardless of what they did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7892-malraza","name":"Malraza","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-21T11:18:23-08:00","id":1052647,"title":"","content":"Cool<br /> The problem was I didn't think read your last words: hunt them a hahaha my bad<br /> Anyway, I leave this consequence for the future.. Will be a climax.. That started with this paradox <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T05:24:13-08:00","id":1053144,"title":"","content":"bump<br /> any help? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T07:49:16-08:00","id":1053204,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what you're looking for, you're just saying you don't want to follow the rules of how Paradox works so what non-rule ideas do we have? I mean, if you're throwing the rules out anything goes. The spell turns into a gold fish, badabing, badabum and done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T08:08:34-08:00","id":1053217,"title":"","content":"no, u didn t understand.. i v just said that i'll apply anomalies even if i shouldn t ( because he tried to containe paradox). Not a big deal.<br /> But, in any case, i should apply a condition to him and i m try to create a funny condition that reflect the spell he casted.. i was thinking about a time loop, because he has abused of the &quot;shifting sand&quot;. As i said, he applied 3 reaches on top of the free granted ( and casted already 3 paradoxes in the same scene).<br /> hope is more clear now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:04:41-08:00","id":1053298,"title":"","content":"My suggestion was something akin to the Monster Nemesis Condition from the Alexandrian Dark Era, which assembles a warped creature out of nearby animals to hound the mage's steps until it's killed (no easy task, as it's immune to control by the Arcana) or falls apart (which takes a fair amount of time).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:15:41-08:00","id":1053302,"title":"","content":"A. The character's past has been rewritten. They've experienced something that didn't happen for the rest of reality.<br /> B. The character has been dislodged from time. They may be intermittently replaced by their future or past versions.<br /> C. Their personal perception of time may fluctuate, slowing down or accelerating at inconvenient moments. The effect is nauseating.<br /> D. They may get short bouts of interference from other timelines, from seeing different content on photographs to having conversations with alternate people.<br /> E. Their enemies benefits from localized time loops. An intruder enters a sealed Sanctum; they run to the door and by opening it let the intruder in.<br /> <br /> You can rewrite these to be potentially beneficial. The character might find a way to utilize the time loops.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T10:33:29-08:00","id":1053310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubios</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053204#post1053204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure what you're looking for, you're just saying you don't want to follow the rules of how Paradox works so what non-rule ideas do we have? I mean, if you're throwing the rules out anything goes. The spell turns into a gold fish, badabing, badabum and done.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malraza</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1052646#post1052646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why are you asking about the rules if you want to do something no matter what you learn? If it's what you think is good for the story, the go for it. Keep in mind that doing this even after the player chose how they wanted to deal with the paradox is taking away player agency and choice, railroading them into the story that you want regardless of what they did.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053217#post1053217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no, u didn t understand.. i v just said that i'll apply anomalies even if i shouldn t ( because he tried to containe paradox).</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree, they understand perfectly, and their points are valid. In particular the removal of the players' agency can produce very bad habits in players that the rest of the gaming community and future versions of yourself will have to deal with. My advice? Have player choices matter, if you're going to have house rules have them written down so the players can know them and to keep yourself honest, and don't be overly invested in particular outcomes for the story, other than the vague goal of a story that is entertaining, and/or meaningful.<br /> <br /> As far as Hounds of Tindalos? Possibly make containing more damaging as a house rule to increase the temptation to release the paradox, and wait for the player to make that choice, and then use the Hounds like a set mouse trap. I like to set my plot important temptations so that any member of the group can choose it, because there is always a player character that'll bite something and they drag everyone else into the plot. Setting different temptations that appeal to each player character is also a valid strategy, but could lead to multiple people in the boat having fish on the line to to speak.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-22-2017, 01:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T11:33:59-08:00","id":1053343,"title":"","content":"Why do you say so? I clearly said what the anomaly applied is. This is not a meaningless choice to twist plot. It s important. As I said, changing the subject of the spell by caster from werewolf ( in which they don t trust really much, as I wrote) means that, once he ll back in time, he will need (donno if it s the right verbal time to point an action that will be done in the past, that acts in the future <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) to convince them about what will happen. I don t see it like a cheat. But a way to make story.<br /> A way to improve the feeling about my 2 mages players and the new-come werewolf.. Is it so weird?<br /> And by the way, why so many problem with that? In my second post i wrote the reasons i made this choice. I dont know if you have red it, but seems to be reasonable from my prospective, isn't it?<br /> Maybe, just maybe, I shouldn't have mentioned this particular detail, because the answers received are going in this direction, while my struggle was a paradox conditions good to apply.<br /> <br /> Thus, we r in the first run of mage, we used to play &quot;wod&quot; before and &quot;the masquerade&quot;. On top of that, seems that the second edition has not been translate in my language and my players refused to read the manual (one in particular Doesn't know English).<br /> I explained them rules and if you knew them you would probably agree with my decision to do not explain too many rules. But doesn't t matter. Ain't the thread s task.<br /> <br /> First of all the ideas of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> are what I was looking for. I m gonna arrange them.. For the hounds, instead, I v considered this choice, only if this player will abuse more and more during the chapter<br /> thank you for answers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12670,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","user":"Dante90","date":". 02-22-2017, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:09:02-08:00","id":1053384,"title":"","content":"Ok, I think I need some clarification. Do you want an Anomaly, or do you want a Paradox Condition? An Anomaly is the collective name of Paradoxes that are a result of releasing a spell instead of containing it, so if that isn't what you meant then your word choice was confusing. English doesn't seem to be your first language (I hope that isn't an offensive observation) so it might be my fault for not reading your posts more closely and misunderstanding you. What I got from what you were saying at the beginning is that you wanted to ignore the rules about what happens when a Mage attempts to contain a spell and fails in favor of causing an Anomaly Paradox. In which case I was inclined to be annoyed because it does look like blatant disregard for your players choices, and the rules. Not that there's anything wrong with disregarding the rules when you know what you're doing, but doing it just for the sake of doing it because you think it might be cool 1) Doesn't actually help us help you because we don't know your houserules, and 2) looks like you're being a jerk to your players because they're likely caught by surprise as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T13:31:22-08:00","id":1053397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053343#post1053343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don t see it like a cheat. But a way to make story.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it may not apply too heavily here, I would caution you to make sure that you aren't the only one that feels that way. You might not see it as a cheat yourself, but some of your players <i>might</i>. So again, I caution you to make sure they know <i>for sure</i> that this is a weird thing with a weird cause. Make sure they <i>know</i> this is a Mystery and not the ST's way of just fucking with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:07:34-08:00","id":1053413,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> well.. a bit upset, because i v never had problems talking with people, even in my job...but nevermind. Thought to have expressed my problem clearly, but we can fix easily <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> first of all, on one will be felt cheated.. for some reasons i can't explain. It s not a big deal, i mean: the mage won t be the target of the spell. The effect will be the same (&quot;shifting sands&quot;). I wanna test their roleplaying and this, in my opinion, is the better way to do it. Do you guys think is too much??<br /> <br /> second, i was looking for funny paradox conditions, like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a> wrote.. he got it apparently so..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12670,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","user":"Dante90","date":". 02-22-2017, 05:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:25:42-08:00","id":1053417,"title":"","content":"So, let me just make sure everyone is on the same page here. Your player used Shifting Sands, applying 3 Reach above his free Reach. He contained the Paradox, rolling Wisdom as a contested action against your Paradox dice pool, and you rolled 2 more successes than him.<br /> <br /> You want to make sure Paradox is especially dangerous in your game, so you plan to apply two Reach worth of Anomalies, <i>in addition to</i> the Paradox Condition and any Resistant bashing damage from Wisdom successes. Is this correct?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:32:52-08:00","id":1053425,"title":"","content":"Yes and no. I wanna use only one reach to change target. But is not the point! I m trying to ask a kind of paradox condition that can release a nice consequence.. I can t understand why everybody is focusing on this stuff.. I just mentioned it to explain better the situation..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T14:52:00-08:00","id":1053433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053425#post1053425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. I wanna use only one reach to change target. But is not the point! I m trying to ask a kind of paradox condition that can release a nice consequence.. I can t understand why everybody is focusing on this stuff.. I just mentioned it to explain better the situation..</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, because the whole point of giving the option to release or contain Paradox is to give the player the choice between harming themselves or risking harm to others when they over-reach. If the player chose to contain the Paradox and you apply effects as if they had released it, you're presenting them with a false choice. You're giving them the option to absorb the harm done by their Paradox themselves, and then causing the spell to go haywire anyway.<br /> <br /> Now, if you have a house rule that any Paradox successes on a contained Paradox apply Anomalies in addition to Paradox Conditions, that's fine as long as the players are aware of this house rule, and you apply it consistently. But if you just randomly decide that you're going to change the rules because you feel like it, your players <i>will</i> feel cheated. And rightfully so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:06:40-08:00","id":1053448,"title":"","content":"It s not a Hr. Just a way to test their roleplay.. The change ( repeat: won t be the mage to back in time but the werewolf, the new entry) won t be influence the final result.. <br /> I really can get the point of this problem.. It s OT <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:06:49-08:00","id":1053449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053425#post1053425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna use only one reach to change target. But is not the point! I m trying to ask a kind of paradox condition that can release a nice consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing the target is an Anomaly, a Paradox Condition is a different thing. This is either you not understanding the difference, or not caring and wanting to whap your players over the head with something out of left field. I recommend coming up with an actual Paradox Condition and not ignoring the rules unless you've talked about it with your players and they're cool with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:14:46-08:00","id":1053457,"title":"","content":"I give up. Close the thread. I asked for A, you answered for B. Despite I explained you the situation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:37:21-08:00","id":1053468,"title":"","content":"Don't be surprised if your players will start playing extremely cautiously and avoid any paradox related risks after doing this. One of reasons why Paradox looks like it looks is because old paradox rules reinforced generally unfun gameplay patterns - they punished you for using your powers in interesting ways, and the only reward for playing like that was not being punished. <br /> Current Paradox was modeled with (according to my judgement and analysis) idea in mind that you shouldn't punish mage player for using magic, and that if you make it too dangerous, people will *not* embrace the trope of trying to flirt with the dark side and &quot;totally have it under control&quot; until it blows up in their faces. If there is a 5% risk of Great Old One eating your face on every magic roll, people will generally avoid rolling magic. <br /> <br /> This is why Paradox needs a build up to be scary, and it is pretty containable and controllable at low levels - you totally CAN do the damage control. You CAN play in the danger zone and flirt with the dark side. And when you *do* fail, you will have a choice of either heroically taking it in the guts, or being selfish and releasing it. This is also why Anomalies apply to *the subject of the spell* - you are deciding that someone else than you should suffer consequences of your actions. This is why I advise against making each Released Paradox bite mage in the ass, because...people will simply not release Paradox if that's the case 9 out of 10 times. <br /> <br /> Paradox is manageable until it's not manageable. And curiously, managing Paradox tricks you into gameplay and behavioral patterns that slowly build up Paradox to the point where it might actually stop being manageable before you realize it. Which is exactly what the game wants - &quot;I can totally handle this&quot; doesn't work if you never can handle it. You can handle it until you cannot.<br /> <br /> It's kinda like fights in dungeon crawls - you shouldn't make each combat encounter &quot;deadly hard and challenging&quot;. People need easy and medium hard encounters to give hard encounters context and make them feel hard. If each combat is hard and deadly, people won't &quot;smart up&quot; and &quot;develop better tactics&quot; - they will just figure out how to avoid combats and will associate unfun experience with the actual combating Be careful to not make your Paradox unfun mechanic that will be perceived as a tool to punish them for rolling badly instead of something to play with. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T15:55:10-08:00","id":1053478,"title":"","content":"no one talked about cheating.. i just wanna change this particular thing<br /> it s not the end of world, how you guys are pointing<br /> i recieved tons of replies with all the same things, but only one answered correctly.. i have no words<br /> didn t open a thread obout: is it good if i change the rule this time?<br /> you argumentations are pointless<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:08:20-08:00","id":1053485,"title":"","content":"Just trying to unveil some &quot;behind the curtain&quot; workings of Paradox, and why it looks like it looks. It's important to make informed choices, especially when homeruling. I just feel that if your goal is to make Paradox scary and unattractive, current rule set will not work for you, because it was designed with not only different, but also conflicting goal in mind - to make Paradox tempting and itching to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T16:25:22-08:00","id":1053495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053457#post1053457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I give up. Close the thread. I asked for A, you answered for B. Despite I explained you the situation</div> </div> </div> </div>That'd be because that's not how the rules work, which brings up this whole concern of do you know what you're doing? Because if you don't know, we want to help you get it. It will be easier for us to help you if we're not confused by what you do and don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053478#post1053478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">no one talked about cheating.. i just wanna change this particular thing<br /> it s not the end of world, how you guys are pointing<br /> i recieved tons of replies with all the same things, but only one answered correctly.. i have no words<br /> didn t open a thread obout: is it good if i change the rule this time?<br /> you argumentations are pointless</div> </div> </div> </div>I can understand that it feels like you're being unfairly dog piled, but I think you should look at all of these replies that have a similar theme and ask yourself whether or not your wrong in assuming their irrelevance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-22-2017, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:02:58-08:00","id":1053516,"title":"","content":"Well.. I said several time in previous posts that I KNOW how should suppose to work.. But people seem to write without read and pretend to be right... <br /> At this point I m start to believe that no one red the entire post but just replied after seen last post.. <br /> If you can t understand what the thread is asking about.. I don t know what to say anymore.. Your only problem is how should work and not what I asked. And, after 20 posts you all insist on this when I already explained, several times, my argumentation.. Not once<br /> Now I ask you: do you even know what I asked? <br /> I don t wanna upset nobody, don t get me wrong, but it s a really weird thread right now. Only one person gave me an answer.. <br /> I know it s not the rule.. But I don t care. There is no police department for who doesn't t use the rule strictly.. I am a player who always use the rules, but, if, sometimes, to make story, I can change something, I don t care. And this is a good opportunity. <br /> I hope this time the explanation is better, even for the next guy that will come and read the last reply. <br /> Still, after 2 pages, there are no good answers, except one. The sense of the topic is gone for good I think","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:19:00-08:00","id":1053525,"title":"","content":"As I pointed out, I was actually confused about what you were asking for because you say you want an anomaly, but then talk about it as a Paradox Condition and these are not the same thing. You've talked about them like they are the same thing though, so how am I supposed to respond if I don't even know what you're talking about and I don't even know if you know what you're talking about?<br /> <br /> When I did think I knew what you were talking about and that you also knew what you were talking about I suggested just doing whatever the hell you wanted because you're purposely ignoring the rules. Once you start to do that though it becomes more difficult to help you nail down something specific because I don't know what you're doing on account of you're no longer using the base language of the rules that we could both have a chance of understanding and are instead crafting your own dialect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-22-2017, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:24:59-08:00","id":1053526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053516#post1053516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well.. I said several time in previous posts that I KNOW how should suppose to work.. But people seem to write without read and pretend to be right... <br /> At this point I m start to believe that no one red the entire post but just replied after seen last post.. <br /> If you can t understand what the thread is asking about.. I don t know what to say anymore.. Your only problem is how should work and not what I asked. And, after 20 posts you all insist on this when I already explained, several times, my argumentation.. Not once<br /> Now I ask you: do you even know what I asked? <br /> I don t wanna upset nobody, don t get me wrong, but it s a really weird thread right now. Only one person gave me an answer.. <br /> I know it s not the rule.. But I don t care. There is no police department for who doesn't t use the rule strictly.. I am a player who always use the rules, but, if, sometimes, to make story, I can change something, I don t care. And this is a good opportunity. <br /> I hope this time the explanation is better, even for the next guy that will come and read the last reply. <br /> Still, after 2 pages, there are no good answers, except one. The sense of the topic is gone for good I think</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we understand what you are asking. You want help coming up with a Paradox Condition to give your player as a result of two Paradox successes on a contained Paradox. However, you have also stated that you are going to apply an Anomaly to that spell. Normally, contained Paradoxes do not cause Anomalies, so people asked to clarify, to make certain that you are aware that's not how the rule is supposed to work. When you answered, you made it clear that you do know this is a deviation from the rules, but that it is not a house rule you have made your players aware of, and intend to apply consistently.<br /> <br /> Where I'm from, there's a name for when the GM changes the rules at random with no warning and with no consistent pattern to how they change the rules. We call that a screwjob. Most people who have played RPGs for any significant length of time have had the misfortune of playing under a GM who throws random screwjobs at them, and it sucks. It's not fun. And while GMs who do that don't have to answer to any &quot;RPG police&quot;, they do have to answer to their players. If the players feel screwed over by the GM, they will either find a different GM or they will stop playing. The reason you're getting so many responses cautioning you not to randomly apply Anomalies on contained Paradoxes just because you want to and think it'll be a good &quot;roleplaying challenge&quot; is that we sympathize with your players, and we want to convince you not to screw them over like this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 02-22-2017, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:43:30-08:00","id":1053537,"title":"","content":"and even if?? <br /> i play with them since i was 14.. now i am 27.. will someone be upset for this?<br /> no, because they don t care<br /> i clarified before? yes<br /> once? no, 3 or 4 times<br /> you are still point on this. If you are happy i won t apply the first anomaly.. well.. no more funny stuff that will take 15 minutes of roleplay away without changing litteraly nothing<br /> the effect will be only this: spend 15 minutes.. for a greater good: having good time.. the first rule of all roleplaying sistem, the one that was called &quot;gold rule&quot;<br /> i repeat, is my problem<br /> btw, if, for something like this, a group of players stop playing with a ST, well.. seem to be in 15 years old groudging kid reunion<br /> i'm pretty impressed<br /> 3 pages full of the same stuff, that, to be onest, is pretty OT<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:51:05-08:00","id":1053542,"title":"","content":"Knowing that could have gone a long way to assuring people that you have a good rapport with your group and they're familiar with your style as an ST so they won't feel this is out of character or confusing with what they'd expect from the game.<br /> <br /> Still doesn't fix the communication issue you're having with the forum in general by making it unclear what you actually want. I mean is it an anomaly or a Paradox Condition? Both combined? Something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:55:41-08:00","id":1053544,"title":"","content":"paradox condition my friend, only this one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T17:58:13-08:00","id":1053547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053537#post1053537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 pages full of the same stuff, that, to be onest, is pretty OT</div> </div> </div> </div>And you've spent almost as long griping about it.<br /> <br /> You've apparently gotten the answer you wanted in Teatime's list of suggestions (and apparently my suggestion just <i>doesn't count</i> for reasons which are unclear and possibly nonexistent rather than being of a different tenor than what you're going for), so the only thing to be gained from continuing to argue with people who have no direct influence over your game is that you get more off-topic posts to complain about.<br /> <br /> Do you want more examples of Paradox Conditions that might apply to the use of time travel to circumvent an allied werewolf's inadvertent notification of a graveyard-going adversary through ghostly informants? Because you're going to get more of that from providing additional context than you are from engaging in argument over Storytelling styles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:15:03-08:00","id":1053551,"title":"","content":"Well you r right. <br /> Your idea is brilliant, and as I said, I like to use it later, not now because I don t wanna fire all bullets too fast.. Like a crescent climax. Also, if some events will go according to plans ( my players won t investigate carefully, or they won t consider the idea to be hunted) they will be threat. <br /> But in any good story, timing is important. This particular spell casted has created a good resonance and obviously, someone can track them down ( if he ll discover what happened there). <br /> My starting point, right now, is to create a soft condition. A taste of a mess created by time Arcanum. <br /> For example: my players used to think to become someone like &quot;death eater&quot; from Harry Potter. In the beginning I was planning to create a condition based on this: images of the future, in which they act like death eater, enslaving sleepers for example. I could make them taste what their actions would bring them if they follow this path. <br /> But wasn't the sure if this idea could be considered a paradox condition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-22T18:31:32-08:00","id":1053562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053544#post1053544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">paradox condition my friend, only this one</div> </div> </div> </div>Abyssal Time: A character's attempt to travel back in time has gone badly awry and his temporal Presence has become unstuck, when the time travel spell ends the changes he made aren't Lasting and he won't rejoin the Present but will instead project ahead of it for the Duration of the Condition. The Present will carry on as if he has suddenly vanished, but the Mage will observe it all as a grim pre-determination they can do nothing about except to try and go back again.<br /> <br /> Resolution: Successfully casting a spell that allows the Mage to travel through Time, forward or backward without further Paradox, or allowing the Condition to Lapse, or Scouring the Condition from their Pattern.<br /> <br /> ~<br /> <br /> Basically, the idea here is that the Mage can ride the Condition out and rejoin the Present but things may have gone a way that he wouldn't approve of while he was stuck. Alternatively, the Mage can cut his losses, Scour the Condition and rejoin the Present now. Alternatively, he can use Time to go back again (But now has to go further if he wants to fix everything and not just his magic mistake), and probably risks even more Paradox, although a quick fix would be to shoot forward in time and miss out completely on whatever happens while he's gone and arrive in a time with no certain knowledge of what's happened during his absence as would happen if he just rode the Condition out.<br /> <br /> Since it's a Paradox Condition I tailored it to effect a Mage, and not the werewolf, but hey you're going to house rule anyway, so good luck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T05:59:28-08:00","id":1053774,"title":"","content":"That s a really good idea. Can be a starting point for interesting plot. <br /> Just a clarification : does the player know how to resolve the condition ( aside from scouring it)?<br /> Edit : to create a good plot, the anomaly is pointless. Good point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12670,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","user":"Dante90","date":". 02-23-2017, 09:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:04:34-08:00","id":1053776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053774#post1053774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That s a really good idea. Can be a starting point for interesting plot. <br /> Just a clarification : does the player know how to resolve the condition ( aside from scouring it)?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's your call, but I'd let them know or let them know the best way to research it. If the player doesn't know about it though then they only have two options to Scour or let it lapse and you lose out on them having the ability to try and resolve the Condition via more time travel.<br /> <br /> Also, I wouldn't really consider it a starting point for a plot, it's just an obstacle that crops up during the course of the plot like pretty much all Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T06:52:19-08:00","id":1053792,"title":"","content":"Ye.. I m overthinking <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> When you have said suddenly vanish, did you mean that in the present he is no longer physically there?<br /> Or simply he can only see what will happen like a spectator?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12670,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","user":"Dante90","date":". 02-23-2017, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:05:38-08:00","id":1053797,"title":"","content":"From outside perspective it will be like he used Temporal Stutter on himself. So to observers he'll have just disappeared and will reappear at a later time either almost immediately by Scouring or using Temporal Stutter (Which would cause him to lose at least a turn), or by allowing the Condition to lapse in which case depending on Wisdom he could be gone anywhere from a turn to a month.<br /> <br /> From the Mage's perspective think Ghost of Christmas Presejt or Past, he's there and can move around and observe but no one can notice or interact with him. He can't influence events just has to watch them unfold unless he successfully uses Time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:29:06-08:00","id":1053810,"title":"","content":"Cool.. It s what I was looking for. Need to practice better to understand how to use conditions properly.<br /> <br /> Maybe I can give him some clues to resolve the condition, with some rolls.. Perhaps occult? <br /> <br /> And last thing. Hope I ll be clear. After the spell is cast, only he will know the informations they gather of course, but when he backs in time, and vanishes, the version of himself In the past should know those informations as well?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:39:17-08:00","id":1053812,"title":"","content":"It's the people in the Present that will perceive the Mage vanishing, the people in the past won't see that happen. The Condition effectively doesn't kick in until after your time travel spell is over and you're supposed to rejoin the Present and essentially overshoot and the price of that is that what you changed in the past doesn't stay changed like it ought to, and you get stuck watching events unfold in the Present with only a small window of opportunity to make things go the way you want. That small window, essentially, is that you have to go back again with the same or an increased risk of Paradox striking again. You could go back less far (Thus not risking Paradox), but then that stuff you were trying to change that didn't change because of the initial Paradox remains unchanged.<br /> <br /> The Condition delivers an array of options, go all the way back and try all over again and risk further Paradox, or use any of multiple other options to accept that you can't go back and change the thing you were trying to change. Since you're gone from the Present for the Duration determined by the time you have for the Condition before it lapses you also start losing the ability to affect the Present or Future unless you attempt magic or Scouring to resolve the Condition and even then you'll lose at least one turn of time which in a high stress environment could be pretty damaging to your cabal or situation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 02-23-2017, 10:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T07:48:15-08:00","id":1053816,"title":"","content":"Fine. Really thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T09:14:59-08:00","id":1053850,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053776#post1053776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the player doesn't know about it though then they only have two options to Scour or let it lapse</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that these seem to be <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029936#post1029936\">functionally the same thing</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T09:37:44-08:00","id":1053856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053850#post1053850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth noting that these seem to be <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1029550-what-happens-when-a-paradox-condition-lapses?p=1029936#post1029936&amp;quot;]functionally</a> the same thing[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>True, it's basically a matter of timing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-23T11:54:38-08:00","id":1053927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053526#post1053526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where I'm from, there's a name for when the GM changes the rules at random with no warning and with no consistent pattern to how they change the rules. We call that a screwjob. Most people who have played RPGs for any significant length of time have had the misfortune of playing under a GM who throws random screwjobs at them, and it sucks. It's not fun. And while GMs who do that don't have to answer to any &quot;RPG police&quot;, they do have to answer to their players. If the players feel screwed over by the GM, they will either find a different GM or they will stop playing. The reason you're getting so many responses cautioning you not to randomly apply Anomalies on contained Paradoxes just because you want to and think it'll be a good &quot;roleplaying challenge&quot; is that we sympathize with your players, and we want to convince you not to screw them over like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perfectly worded to capture the sentiment I was thinking when I wrote this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In particular the removal of the players' agency can produce very bad habits in players that the rest of the gaming community and future versions of yourself will have to deal with. My advice? Have player choices matter, if you're going to have house rules have them written down so the players can know them and to keep yourself honest, and don't be overly invested in particular outcomes for the story, other than the vague goal of a story that is entertaining, and/or meaningful.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053537#post1053537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and even if??<br /> i play with them since i was 14.. now i am 27.. will someone be upset for this?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12670\" data-vbnamecard=\"12670\">Dante90</a> Especially since you've been role-playing since you were 14 you should know what we are saying about Storytellers governing their games like a pre-Magna Carta fiefdom is true and if you don't that means you're likely the one oblivious to that style of play, and the likely source of that experience for some people. (Assuming you're not roleplaying in an isolated bubble, which happens and is unfortunate, and my apologies if that's the case) This all refers back to this question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1052537-help-with-paradox-of-time-arcanum?p=1053495#post1053495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can understand that it feels like you're being unfairly dog piled, but I think you should look at all of these replies that have a similar theme and ask yourself whether or not your wrong in assuming their irrelevance.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're pulling out our gaming anyone-can-say-anything-on-the-internet unverifiable credentials, I've been a DM, GM, Referee, Lore Master, CryptKeeper, and Storyteller since I was 10 and am current 38 (28 years). I've put more time and effort into roleplay than most college professors, lawyers, or doctors put into their particular fields in a equivalent range of years (most being defined by those who put in average time/effort, and those that put in less totaled). Please don't take my remarks as intending to disrupt or harm, their intent is to share things I and others had to learn the hard way, to avoid making bitter players, and help you consider player choices as valid and meaningful, because they should be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 02-24-2017, 10:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}